# Choose your path

**Prerequisites:** you can use a terminal and read code.
**You will do:** skip the foundation you already have.
**Time:** one page.
**Next:** the matching primer, then [Rocci in five minutes](/docs/start/five-minutes/).

Every path converges on the same first component. Do not start the
application tutorial until that component previews.

## I know Roc

You already write modules, records, tags, and `!` effects. Read
[Web foundations for Roc authors](/docs/start/web-foundations/) so HTML, HTTP
methods, fragments, and Datastar morphing are not surprises. Then
[install](/docs/start/install/) if needed and run
[Rocci in five minutes](/docs/start/five-minutes/).

## I know web development

You already know HTML, CSS, forms, and HTTP. Read
[Roc for Rocci authors](/docs/start/roc-for-rocci/) for the Roc subset later
examples use. Then [install](/docs/start/install/) and
[Rocci in five minutes](/docs/start/five-minutes/).

## I know both

Skip the primers. [Install](/docs/start/install/) if this machine has no
checkout, then [Rocci in five minutes](/docs/start/five-minutes/) and
[Build your first component](/docs/tutorials/first-component/).

## After the first component

The next controlled project is a standalone counter with SQLite and a one-shot
`@post:fragment`. That tutorial ships in the application journey. Until then, the
canonical complete source is [Styling](/examples/styling/).
